//
// @C124 (formal/binding.md D-bind-45) — a `const` value reaches only a `const` parameter, and
// otherwise the call is refused (`const-to-plain-parameter`).  A plain record or collection parameter
// names the caller's value (`calls.md` F-ParamHeap), so a `const` value handed to one could be
// written by the callee: `bump(acct)` below changed the caller's balance to 999 on both backends while
// `acct.balance = 1` was refused.  The decision is by the SIGNATURE, never the callee's body —
// `show(acct)` is refused although `show` only reads, because what a call means is judged from the
// call and the declaration it names (C121), and a proof that a callee does not write stays an
// optimisation's to use (C122).  It shipped as a warning while the libraries declared their
// read-only parameters `const`; every shipped library has, so it is the error the decision states.
//
// Every spelling a parameter can be reached by is a cell: a plain function, a read-only one, a
// view handed on, the standard library's `clear` (which writes), a `self` method in both call
// spellings, and a generic.  The legal side — `const` parameters, the stdlib's readers, text and
// scalars, an interface bound — is `a-const-value-passed-to-a-const-parameter-is-legal.loft`.
// Every cell here is refused, so the file has no entry point and runs nothing.
//
// @falsified-by: tests/falsified/c124-the-plain-parameter-error.patch — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/7 -> 0/7 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches), native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/7 -> 0/7 (the suite's verdict, not a count of matches)
//   CHANNEL: expectations — the control is this tree with the three `const-to-plain-parameter`
//   sites back at `Level::Warning`, where every pin is unmet because nothing is refused.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass const parameter 'acct' to parameter 1 `a` of `bump1542`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass const parameter 'acct' to parameter 1 `a` of `show1542`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass 'f', a view of const parameter 'accts', to parameter 1 `a` of `show1542`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass const parameter 'v' to parameter 1 `self` of `clear`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass const parameter 'acct' to parameter 1 `self` of `peek1542`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass const parameter 'acct' to parameter 1 `self` of `look1542`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot pass const parameter 'v' to parameter 1 `v` of `first1542`

struct Acc1542 { balance: integer }

fn bump1542(a: Acc1542) { a.balance = 999; }
fn show1542(a: Acc1542) -> integer { a.balance }
fn peek1542(self: Acc1542) -> integer { self.balance }
fn look1542(self: Acc1542) -> integer { self.balance }
fn first1542<T>(v: vector<T>) -> T? { v[0] }

// a callee that writes its parameter
fn writer(acct: const Acc1542) { bump1542(acct); }

// a callee that only reads, but does not say so
fn reader(acct: const Acc1542) -> integer { show1542(acct) }

// a view of a const collection handed on
fn view_on(accts: const vector<Acc1542>) -> integer {
  s = 0;
  for f in accts { s += show1542(f); }
  s
}

// the standard library's `clear` writes, and stays plain
fn wipe(v: const vector<integer>) { clear(v); }

// a `self` method
fn method_self(acct: const Acc1542) -> integer { acct.peek1542() }

// a `self` method called in its FUNCTION spelling (C123: `self` gives a name both call spellings)
fn both_form(acct: const Acc1542) -> integer { look1542(acct) }

// a generic
fn generic(v: const vector<integer>) -> integer { first1542(v) ?? 0 }
